    "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Hyperplane",
    "problem": "Find the equation of the tangent hyperplane to the hypersurface $w=4x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(yz)$ at the point $(-1,1,1,-\\pi ).$",
    "worked_solution": "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the hypersurface $w=f(x,y,z)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0},{w}_{0})$ on the hypersurface can be written as\n\n$$\nw-{w}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(z-{z}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂z}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(yz))=4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(yz) \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(yz))=\\frac{4xz}{1+{y}^{2}{z}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(4x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(yz))=\\frac{4xy}{1+{y}^{2}{z}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y,z)=(-1,1,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(-1,1,1) & =4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1\\cdot 1)=\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(-1,1,1) & =\\frac{4(-1)(1)}{1+({1}^{2})({1}^{2})}=-2 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}(-1,1,1) & =\\frac{4(-1)(1)}{1+({1}^{2})({1}^{2})}=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent hyperplane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-(-\\pi ) & =(x-(-1))\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(-1,1,1)+(y-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(-1,1,1)+(z-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂z}(-1,1,1) \\\\ w+\\pi  & =\\pi (x+1)-2(y-1)-2(z-1) \\\\ w+\\pi  & =\\pi x-2y-2z+4+\\pi  \\\\ \\pi x-2y-2z-w+4 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
